# AGENTS.md — <PROJECT NAME>

> A cross-tool instruction file that many AI agents read natively (Claude Code,
> GitHub Copilot, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Aider, …). This is your *single source of
> truth* when more than one AI works on the project — the modern version of the shared
> `.md` context you already maintain.
>
> Strategy: keep the real content here in `AGENTS.md`. Point `CLAUDE.md` at it so you
> only maintain ONE file. On Windows the simplest is to keep `CLAUDE.md` as a one-liner:
>
> ```
> See AGENTS.md for all project rules and context.
> ```
> (or copy the content into both; or use a directory junction.)

